course: dictionary
lesson: 10559
title: Unchanged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unchanged means not changed; it is still the same as before. The start un- means not, so unchanged is the opposite of changed. If something is still the way it was, it is unchanged.
explain: «Most of the rest is nitrogen, which we breathe in and out unchanged.» Nitrogen goes into your body and comes back out still nitrogen. It has not been turned into anything new, so unchanged means it stays the same.
explain: In science, the things you keep unchanged are called controlled variables, so the test stays fair. «The weather remained unchanged» means the weather stayed the same.
explain: Watch for the phrases «remain unchanged», «stay unchanged» and «left unchanged». They all mean the same thing: nothing was altered.
fact: Unchanged means not changed; still the same as before.
fact: Un- at the start means not, so unchanged is the opposite of changed.
fact: «Stayed almost unchanged» means it stayed nearly the same for a very long time.
fact: In maths, a number multiplied by 1 stays unchanged.
fact: Useful phrases: «remain unchanged», «stay unchanged», «left unchanged».
exercise: «Most of the rest is nitrogen, which we breathe in and out unchanged.» What does unchanged mean here? | Hidden inside the lungs | Changed into something new | *Not changed, still the same | Very cold
exercise: In maths, a number multiplied by 1 stays unchanged. What does that mean? | It disappears | It becomes zero | *Its value stays the same | It doubles
exercise: «The old road has stayed unchanged for years.» Which phrase could replace unchanged without changing the meaning? | brand new | *still the same | painted red | moved away
test: Which phrase means the same as «left unchanged»? | Completely rebuilt | Painted over | *Still as it was | Given away
test: «Lisbon is the capital, and the border has remained unchanged since 1297.» What does remained unchanged tell you about the border? | It was built last week | *It has stayed the same | It has been moved | It is being argued about
exam: Which sentence uses unchanged correctly? | The dog unchanged jumped the fence | *The river looked unchanged after a hundred years | Unchanged, the cup was broken | The bread was unchanged, so it was baked
